It's been a long time since I started playing nethack. I heard
somewhere about rogue, a text-based game, and decided to give it a
try, since I like RPG's. So I played rogue and i liked it quite, but I
also heard about Nethack, a rogue-like game whitch had been in
development for 15 years, none of the effort on the graphical
interface, all into gameplay...

So this way I started dying and dying for two or three years, until
yesterday. The most near I've always been was an orcish barbarian
named hate who was killed by Rodney; he actually hadn't an ascension
kit, so this time I decided take it more seriously. Other remarkable
attempts all finished in YASD: the priest killed when trying to
convert a lawful altar sacrificing a white unicorn, the monk who
decided it was a good idea to have a taste of medusa, the barbarian
who slid over a boulder in sokoban and found a chickatrice... run for
the lizard corpse... too late!. Countless :-).

The key of this game was the wand of death I had as initial item and 3
altars on the higher levels. I arrived minetown and found a bones
file, another guy who was going to buy protection from a cross-aligned
priest and somehow managed to get him angry; luckily for me the priest
was co-aligned, so I started sacrificing. The bones pile had actually
nothing useful, then, suddently, came something nasty (i can't
remember what, i didn't take notes). I was about to die on an early
runnaway when something was triggered in my head: "You, stupid, use
that /oD!!!!".
So I survived. Later i found a polymorph trap, any my pet turned into
a silver dragon!. I went to minetown and let him feed from the
shoopkepers, a good diet for dragons. This way I got some money to buy
protection from the priest. Protection whitch I managed to lose due to
not respecting prayer timeout not once, but twice (I never learn, I
have not enough patience!).
Somehow the dragon got killed, he left no scales, I had to go with a
crystal plate mail from one of minetown guards, too many weight, but
allowed me to survive until I found later a set of silver dragon
scales.
By then I had managed to get teleportitis. Headed to sokoban by
stages, doing a level, returning to minetown for some praying... and
finally the price, a bag of holding.
The quest was no pain, I actually don't remember anything.
Going down heading for medusa I found a temple with a lawful priest. I
headed out of the temple and in the corridor a chickatrice came for
me. I killed'er and she let a corpse... RNG, are you trying to say
something to me?? -Actually yes... DO IT!!-. So I took the chickatrice
corpse and petrified the priest. The guy had a spellbook of finguer of
death, not bad :-).
Two levels or three below was another altar, on level 21. My campbase.
A level below of it there was a co-aligned priest and on the next one
there was another. By sacrificing got a spellbook of create monster,
and then started the real carnage. When I was sure enough went for
medusa, with a ring of levitation, a blindfold and a mirror. She was
no match.
Got almost all spellbooks, so I started a polipylling frenzy to get
the stuff. I could actually have done a wishless conduct, since I got
all what I needed from polipilling, but preferred not to force too
mutch for the first ascension.
I also had a phase of taming, I was collecting dragons by their color;
also had two angels, a titan, a Kirin... feeding them was fun. Had an
accident with one of the two priests below the camp, charmed a
titanothere on the temple whitch killed him before i could say "stop
it, you naughty!".
As usual, sacrificed some orcs; I never remember not to do it, so
Yehenogu and Jubilex came. Just killed them.
Got my ascension kit, but I managed to break two +4 T-shirts, a +4
oilskin cloak and a +4 cloak of protection in polymorphing accidents
(You turn to a Silver dragon... DAMN!). Finally Used a Robe and a
small shield. I had a Shield of reflection ready for ascending (It was
told that the amulet of yendor drains power, so I supposed I would
have not been able to cast spells. I supposed wrong).
Did a mistake, mispelled "enchant weapon" for "enchant armor", so my
lovely werebane, whitch used to cut succubus like butter (succubus
remember me of a girlfriend I used to have... ), was gone in the blink
of an eye.
Genocided most annoyig L's, h's and ;'s. Discovered the joy of having
a purple worm as a pet. Headed to Rodney, With those speed boots, helm
of brilliance, amulet of life saving... froze the water surronding his
lair, killed him with a fast finger of death...
And the hellhound breathed fire.
Oh, where has the book of the dead gone?
Well, time for a bath, took out the "oLS and used magical breathing.
Don't know why I took Rodney's corpse out of the moat, but I did
actually.
Then I became really paranoid, everytime I saw a purple @ I started
casting finger of death like a madman... poor Elvenking... heheheh!
The mysterious force was quite annoying. The planes were no really
great pain; plain of water was a bit boring, but let me recover all Pw
and Hp.
So I was about to face the final test. Right famine, left pestilence,
Death awaiting in front of me. I had lots of food, so I went to make a
little visit to the hungry one. Lawful; I actually had a helm of
opposite alignment, but what kind of orc is lawful??? (Chaos rules!).
So, headed for pestilence, two or three appliances for the unicorn
horn to find out that the altar was neutral. Well, neutral is good
enough, but I wanted something special for the first time, you know.
Death, aaah, they say you suck hit points like a succucus sucks...
ahem. What I was talking about? Yes, headed in front, death on my
left, and some insects over there. Charmed some of them, death sent me
her finger (thanks, robe plus magicbane!), put some giant ants between
us, zapped a /oD to the annoying priest in front of me...
This time the altar is chaotic
What do you want to sacrifice?
y (the amulet of Yendor named the real one).

